        },
        {
            "name": "Abraham Rosenfeld (translation)",
            "bio": "Abraham Isaac Jacob Rosenfeld (1914-1984), born in Jerusalem, was a rabbi, army chaplain, and ḥazzan in the United Kingdom. He studied at the Yeshivah Etz Ḥayyim and Merkaz ha-Rav in Jerusalem. He came to the UK in 1934 to take up the post of chazan at Walford Road Synagogue, Stoke Newington, London. In 1941, he began serveing as both rabbi and ḥazzan to the Finchley Synagogue in London and was appointed honorary president of the Cantors' Association of England. He obtained semikhah from Israel in the 1950s. In 1970, he was appointed rabbi of the congregation of Wellington, New Zealand and laid the foundation stone of the community center there in 1974. He returned to Israel in 1978. He briefly assisted the Edgware United Synagogue as acting rabbi before he retired to Jerusalem, Israel in 1980. His translation into English of the Seliḥot service (1956) and the Kinot for the Tishah b'Av (1965) received the approbation of the chief rabbi of England, Rabbi Sir Israel *Brodie. He composed a special memorial prayer for the victims of the Holocaust which can be found in his Kinot for Tishah b'Av. He was President of the Finchley commission of the Jewish National Fund and Joint Israel Appeal committee. A JNF forest in the western Negev was named after him and also a library in Wellington.",
            "website": "",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/abraham-rosenfeld-96x96.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/abraham-rosenfeld"
        },
        {
            "name": "Shlomo Fundaminsky",
            "bio": "Dr. Shlomo Fundaminsky (span class=\"hebrew\"&gt;שלמה פונדמינסקי</span>; fl. 20th c.) was a Hebrew poet, grammarian and Jewish educator in the United Kingdom. He worked for years at the London Board for Jewish Religious Education. An old-school religious masqil, he wrote the standard Hebrew grammar book used in the UK Jewish education system: <em> A New Hebrew Grammar </em> (1954), as well as other Modern Hebrew instructional materials. If you know more about Dr. Fundaminsky's life and career, please <a href=\"/contact/\">contact us</a>.",
            "website": "",
            "avatar": "https://opensiddur.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/11/Keith-Evans-Green-Tree-Yellow-Field-CC-BY-SA-250x250.jpg",
            "profile_link": "https://opensiddur.org/profile/shlomo-fundaminsky"
        }
    ],
    "date": "2026-10-23",
    "last_updated": "2026-10-26",
    "excerpt": "This is a qinah piyyut for the victims of the Holocaust by Shlomo Fundaminsky, edited by Abraham Rosenfeld and included in the latter's <em>Authorised Selichot for the Whole Year</em> (1956) in the section on seliḥot for the Fast of Tevet. ",
    "content": "<table style=\"margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\" class=\"draggable toggleable-table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th id=\"x\" style=\"text-align: right;\">Source (Hebrew)</th>\n<th style=\"text-align: left;\">Translation (English)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<span class=\"instruction\">The following verses are intoned by the Reader and repeated by the Congregation</span>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאֱׄלֹהֵינוּ וֵאלֹהֵי אֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nבּׄוֹרְׄאֵֽנוּ וְצוּר יְשׁוּעָתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nהַׄבִּֽיטָה מִׄמְּרוֹמֶֽיךָ וּרְאֵה בְעָנְיֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nO <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span> and <span class=\"divine-referent\">God of our fathers</span>,<br />\n<span class=\"divine-referent\">our Creator</span> and <span class=\"divine-referent\">Rock of our salvation</span>,<br />\nlook down from thy heights and see our affliction\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאָתָֽאנוּ לְפָנֶֽיךָ בְּשִׁבְרוֹן לִבֵּֽנוּ,<br />\nדְָּפַֽקְנוּ דְלָתֶֽיךָ בְּדִכְאוֹן רוּחֵנוּ,<br />\nהַאֲזִֽינָה לְקוֹל תַּחֲנוּנֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWe come before thee with a broken heart,<br />\nwe knock at thy doors with a crushed spirit,<br />\nO hearken to the voice of our supplication.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nלִבֵּֽנוּ נִשְׁבַּר בְּקִרְבֵּֽנוּ,<br />\nכַּחֲלִילִים יֶחֱמוּ מֵעֵֽינוּ,<br />\nבְּזָכְרֵֽנוּ שֵׁשׁ מֵאוֹת רִבּוֹא חֲלָלֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOur heart is broken within us,<br />\nour bowels moan like flutes,<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_1');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[1]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Flutes which produce wailing tones. cf. M.D. on Jer. 48.36. a. Lem. 1.2.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_1').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_1', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script><br />\nwhen we recall our six million slain.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nלִזְאֵבֵי־אָדָם נִמְכְּרוּ אַחֵֽינוּ,<br />\nלִפְרִיצֵי־חַיּוֹת נִמְסְרוּ אַחְיוֹתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nטֶֽרֶף לְחֶלְאַת־הָאָדָם הָיוּ עוֹלָלֵֽינוּ וְטַפֵּֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOur brothers were sold to human wolves,<br />\nour sisters were delivered to ferocious beasts,<br />\nour infants and babes became a prey to the dregs of mankind.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמָֽוֶת שְׁכֹל וְאַלְמוֹן עָלוּ בְּחַלּוֹנֵֽינוּ,<br />\nהוֹרִים וְטִפּוּחֵיהֶם נִשְׂרְפוּ לְעֵינֵֽינוּ,<br />\nוּבְחַדְרֵי־גָז גָּוְעוּ בְּאֶחָד אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nDeath, bereavement and widowhood penetrated our windows,<br />\nparents with their tender children were burnt before our own eyes,<br />\nand with the Shema<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_2');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[2]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Lit. (with) one is <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span>.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_2').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_2', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> (on their lips) they perished in the gas chambers.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמְאוֹרוֹת יִשְׂרָאֵל כָּבוּ בִּמְעוֹנוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nאַרְזֵי הַלְּבָנוֹן שֹׁרְשוּ מִקִּרְבֵּֽנוּ,<br />\nבַּאֲנִי מַאֲמִין נִגְדְּעוּ בְּמִקְדָּשֵֽׁינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nThe lamps of Israel were extinguished in our dwellings,<br />\nthe cedars of Lebanon were uprooted from our midst,<br />\nwith (the singing of) “I Believe,”<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_3');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[3]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> i.e., the belief in the coming of the Messiah. v. A.P.B., p. 95.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_3').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_3', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> they were cut down in our sanctuaries.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nלְשׁוֹנֵֽנוּ דָבְקָה לְחִכֵּֽנוּ,<br />\nמְקוֹר דִּמְעָה הָיוּ עֵינֵֽינוּ,<br />\nוְכוֹס הַיְגוֹנִים רִוְּתָה נַפְשֵֽׁנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nOur tongue cleaves to our palate,<br />\nour eyes are a fount of tears,<br />\nand our soul has drunk in full the cup of sorrow.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nלָֽמָּה עֲזַבְתָּֽנוּ אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ,<br />\nלָמָּה עָמַֽדְתָּ מֵרָחוֹק בְּעֵת צָרָתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nלָֽמָּה הֶחֱרַֽשְׁתָּ עֵת שָׁפְכוּ הֶעָרִיצִים כַּמַּֽיִם דָּמֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhy didst thou forsake us, O <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span>?<br />\nWhy didst thou stand afar at the time of our distress?<br />\nWhy didst thou keep silent when the tyrants spilled our blood like water?\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאֵיפֹה נִמְצָא מָזוֹר לִפְצָעֵֽינוּ,<br />\nמֵאַֽיִן יָבֹֽאוּ נִחוּמִים לְאֶבְלֵֽנוּ,<br />\nאֵיכָֽכָה נִשְׁכַּח אֶת מַחְמַדֵּֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWhere can we find a remedy for our wounds?<br />\nWhence shall comfort come for our mourning?<br />\nHow can we forget our beloved ones?\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאֲבֵלִים נוֹתַֽרְנוּ בְּשִׁמְמָתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nבּוֹדְדִים נִשְׁאַֽרְנוּ בִּיגוֹנֵֽנוּ,<br />\nאוֹיָה כִּי גָדוֹל כַּיָּם שִׁבְרֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nWe remain mourners in our desolation,<br />\nwe were left solitary with our sorrow, woe (to us)!<br />\nFor our calamity is as great as the sea.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nרְאֵה יְיָ חֶרְפָּתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nהַבִּֽיטָה עַל שִׁפְלוּתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nשׁוּר כִּי עַד שְׁאוֹל הוּרַד כְּבוֹדֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSee, O <span class=\"divine-referent\">Lord</span>, our disgrace,<br />\nlook down upon our humiliation,<br />\nbehold how our glory has been brought down to the grave.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nרַחֶם־נָא עַל שְׁרִידֵֽינוּ,<br />\nשִׂים בְּנֹאדְךָ דִמְעוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nנְצֹר בְּאוֹצָרְךָ שֶֽׁפֶךְ־דָּמֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHave mercy, we beseech thee, upon our remnants,<br />\nplace our tears in thy flask,<br />\npreserve in thy storehouse our blood that has been spilled.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nחַיֵּי־נֵֽצַח הַנְחֵל לִקְדוֹשֵֽׁינוּ,<br />\nבִּצְרוֹר הַחַיִּים צְרֹר נִשְׁמוֹת טְהוֹרֵֽינוּ,<br />\nכִּי דָמָם נִשְׁפַּךְ עַל מִזְבַּחֲךָ אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nCause thy<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_4');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[4]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Lit. our.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_4').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_4', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> martyrs to inherit eternal life,<br />\nbind up the souls of our pure ones in the bond of life,<br />\nfor their blood was spilled on thy altar, O <span class=\"divine-referent\">our God</span>.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nחֲמָל־נָא עַל אֲבֵלֵֽנוּ,<br />\nהַצְמַח נִחוּמִים לְאַחֵֽינוּ וּלְאַחְיוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nזְכֹר כִּי הֵם שְׁאֵרִית פְּלֵטָתֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nHave pity, we pray thee, upon our mourners,<br />\ncause comfort to spring forth to our brothers and sisters,<br />\nremember that they are the remnant that has escaped.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמְחֵה בְּרַחֲמֶֽיךָ דִמְעוֹת אֻמְלָלֵֽינוּ,<br />\nהֲפָךְ בְּטוּבְךָ לְשָׂשׂוֹן אֶבְלֵֽנוּ,<br />\nאֱצֹל בְּחַסְדְּךָ מֵהוֹדְךָ עָלֵינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nIn thy mercy wipe away the tears of our unfortunate ones,<br />\nin thy goodness turn our mourning into joy,<br />\nin thy kindness bestow thy splendour upon us.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמָזוֹר וָתֶֽרֶף הַמְצֵא לִפְצָעֵֽינוּ,<br />\nהַעֲלֵה אֲרוּכָה לְכׇל מַכּוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nוְהָרֵם בִּישׁוּעָתְךָ מֵעָפָר קָרְנֵֽנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nBring forth balm and remedy for our wounds,<br />\ngrant healing to all our sores,<br />\nand in thy salvation lift up our pride from the dust.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nיְיָ יְיָ ׀ אֵל רַחוּם וְחַנּוּן שְׁמַע קוֹלֵֽנוּ,<br />\nחוּס וְרַחֵם עֲלֵֽינוּ,<br />\nוְהָשֵׁב שְׁכִינָתְךָ לְצִיּוֹן עִיר קָדְשֵֽׁנוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nO <span class=\"divine-referent\">Lord</span>, O <span class=\"divine-referent\">Lord</span>, Merciful and Gracious <span class=\"divine-referent\">God</span>, hear our voice,<br />\nspare us and have compassion upon us,<br />\nand restore thy divine presence to Ẓíōn, our Holy city.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nיַעֲלֶה לְפָנֶֽיךָ זִכְרוֹן קָרְבְּנוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nיַגִּֽיעַ לְפָנֶֽיךָ קוֹל בְּכִיּוֹת אִמּוֹתֵֽינוּ,<br />\nיִשָּׁמַע בְּאָזְנֶֽיךָ קוֹל דְּמָי תִינוֹקוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nLet the remembrance of our victims come before thee,<br />\nlet the cry of the weeping of our mothers reach thee,<br />\nlet thy ears hearken (to) the cry of the blood of our babes.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמִבְחַר בִּרְכוֹתֶֽיךָ שְׁלַח בְּאַרְצֵֽנוּ,<br />\nמִכׇּל רָע נְצֹר יִשְׂרָאֵל מְדִינָתֵֽנוּ,<br />\nוְהָיְתָה לְגָאוֹן וּלְתִפְאֶֽרֶת כְּמוֹ שֶׁׄהִבְטַֽחְתָּ לַׄאֲבוֹתֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nSend thy choicest blessings to our land,<br />\npreserve the State<span class=\"footnote_referrer\"><a role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" onclick=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" onkeypress=\"footnote_moveToReference__1('footnote_plugin_reference__1_5');\" ><sup id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5\" class=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text\">[5]</sup></a><span id=\"footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5\" class=\"footnote_tooltip\"> Lit. our State.&nbsp;</span></span><script type=\"text/javascript\"> jQuery('#footnote_plugin_tooltip__1_5').tooltip({ tip: '#footnote_plugin_tooltip_text__1_5', tipClass: 'footnote_tooltip', effect: 'fade', predelay: 0, fadeInSpeed: 200, delay: 400, fadeOutSpeed: 200, position: 'center right', relative: true, offset: [0, 0], });</script> of Israel from all evil,<br />\nthat it may become a pride and glory as thou didst promise our fathers.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nמְׄהֵׄרָה יָבוֹא מְשִׁיחֵנוּ,<br />\nלְעֵינֵי כׇל חַי יוֹפִֽיעַ בְּתוֹכֵֽנוּ,<br />\nוְיָצִיץ וְיִפְרַח עַם יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּיָמֵֽינוּ׃\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\nMay our Messiah come speedily,<br />\nmay he appear in our midst in the sight of all living,<br />\nand may the people of Israel blossom and flourish in our own days.\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"liturgy\" lang=\"heb-Hebr\" style=\"text-align: right;\">\nאָמֵן!\n</div>\n</td>\n<td style=\"vertical-align:top;\">\n<div class=\"english\" lang=\"eng-Latn\" style=\"text-align: left;\">\n<em>Amen!</em>\n</div>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<hr />\n<p>This is a qinah piyyut for the victims of the Holocaust by Shlomo Fundaminsky, edited by Abraham Rosenfeld and included in the latter&#8217;s <em><a href=\"/?p=69545\">Authorised Selichot for the Whole Year</a></em> (1956) in the section on seliḥot for the Fast of Tevet. The specific edits made by Rosenfeld aren&#8217;t clear, but the inclusion of his name as an acrostic signature suggests that at least some (besides the acrostic) were substantial.</p>\n<h3>Source(s)</h3>\n<style>\n       .errordiv { padding:10px; margin:10px; border: 1px solid #555555;color: #000000;background-color: #f8f8f8; width:500px; }#advanced_iframe {visibility:visible;opacity:1;vertical-align:top;}.ai-info-bottom-iframe { position: fixed; z-index: 10000; bottom:0; left: 0; margin: 0px; text-align: center; width: 100%; background-color: #ff9999; padding-left: 5px;padding-bottom: 5px; border-top: 1px solid #aaa } a.ai-bold {font-weight: bold;}#ai-layer-div-advanced_iframe p {height:100%;margin:0;padding:0}#ai-div-container-advanced_iframe\n       {\n           position: relative;\n           width: 100%; max-width: 100%;}\n       #ai-div-loader-advanced_iframe\n       {\n          position: absolute;\n          z-index:1000;\n          margin-left:-33px;\n          left: 50%;   top: 150px;\n         }}\n       #ai-div-loader-advanced_iframe img\n       {\n          border: none;\n       }\n\t.ai-fullscreen {\n\t  position:fixed;\n\t  z-index:99999 !important;\n\t  top:0px !important;\n\t  left:0px !important;\n\t  margin:0px !important;\n\t  width:100% !important;\n\t  height:100% !important;\n\t}\n\t.ai-fullscreen-wrapper {\n\t  height: 100vh;\n\t}\n\t